// DYNAMIC.md §4.9: a closure body may be a block with statements, not only a
// single expression. Lua/TS wrap the block in an inline function (an IIFE);
// Python has no multi-statement lambda, so the closure hoists to a nested `def`
// whose statements run *per call* with the parameter in scope — not inlined into
// the enclosing scope and computed once at creation. Calling it twice with
// different arguments proves per-call evaluation: `|n| { let d = n*2; d+1 }`
// gives `stepped(20) == 41` and `stepped(0) == 1`.
extern {
    fn println(n: number);
}

fn main() {
    let stepped = |n| {
        let doubled = n * 2;
        doubled + 1
    };
    println(stepped(20));
    println(stepped(0));
}
